CP31 retained-harness invocation diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-22

Observed artifact:
  A first retained function-scope run with WINEDEBUG=-all terminated with
  SIGSEGV before the contract body.

Diagnosis:
  GDB placed the fault in Wine ntdll init_options(), reading main_argv[1]. The
  retained contract is a dlopen-only process and does not initialize Wine's
  normal argv path. The unchanged CP29 binary reproduces the same fault under
  WINEDEBUG=-all. Both unchanged CP29 and the CP31 candidate pass under the
  contract's original environment.

Conclusion:
  WINEDEBUG=-all is outside this dlopen harness's valid invocation contract.
  It was removed from the matrix. This is an invocation artifact, not a CP31
  source regression. No production change was made in response.
